IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-gaps`

-- je54-tests-gaps: every function of je54-gaps refuses, on every input tried, with the wording that says what the Law does not say.  The expected wording was written from the list in the brief ("What the Law does not say")
-- before this module was run.  One refusal per row of that list, and the rows that take a unit or a date are tried with more than one value to show that no value gets an answer.

§ `A period of days, weeks or years`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the day on which a period that starts on a day ends` (YMD 2020 1 1) 30 `a number of days`
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 has no rule for counting a period of days, weeks or years, and does not say what a day, a week or a year is"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day on which a period that starts on a day ends` (YMD 2020 1 1) 4 `a number of weeks`
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 has no rule for counting a period of days, weeks or years, and does not say what a day, a week or a year is"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day on which a period that starts on a day ends` (YMD 2020 2 29) 1 `a number of years`
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 has no rule for counting a period of days, weeks or years, and does not say what a day, a week or a year is"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day on which a period that starts on a day ends` (YMD 2020 1 1) 0 `a number of days`
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 has no rule for counting a period of days, weeks or years, and does not say what a day, a week or a year is"

§ `The time zone in which a day is read`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the time zone in which the Law reads a day` (YMD 2020 7 1)
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 names no time zone in which a day is read; the caller states the zone, and this row assumes Jersey local time without the Law saying so"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the time zone in which the Law reads a day` (YMD 2020 1 1)
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 names no time zone in which a day is read; the caller states the zone, and this row assumes Jersey local time without the Law saying so"

§ `How long post takes, and the ordinary course of post`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the day on which a letter posted on a day would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` (YMD 2024 3 1)
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 does not say how long post takes or what the ordinary course of post is; the caller states the time at which the letter would be delivered"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day on which a letter posted on a day would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` (YMD 2024 12 24)
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 does not say how long post takes or what the ordinary course of post is; the caller states the time at which the letter would be delivered"

§ `Commencement: the time of day, the 2021 Law, and the Law's own time`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the time of day at which an enactment silent as to the time comes into force, if it is not the start of its day` (YMD 2020 6 10)
        BECAUSE "Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 give the start of the day and no other time of day; the Law gives no other"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day on which an enactment made on or after 28 September 2021 comes into force` (YMD 2021 9 28)
        BECAUSE "the commencement of an enactment made on or after 28 September 2021 is governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day on which an enactment made on or after 28 September 2021 comes into force` (YMD 2026 10 28)
        BECAUSE "the commencement of an enactment made on or after 28 September 2021 is governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment at which the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 came into force`
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 gives no time of day for its own commencement on 21 August 1954"

§ `Which text of Article 8 governs`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8: the text that governs when the day of the event and the day the question is asked fall under different texts` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 10 28)
        BECAUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 does not say whether the text of Article 8 in force on the day of the event or on the day the question is asked governs; ask the function that takes a reading of fork I2"
